    <string name="dcc_approve_download_body">%s (depuis le serveur : %s) vous a envoyé un fichier.\n\nAvertissement : ce téléchargement sera transmis via une connexion non sécurisée et non chiffrée. L’accepter permettra à l’autre personne de voir votre adresse IP. N’acceptez le téléchargement que si vous faites confiance à cet utilisateur.</string>
    <string name="dcc_approve_download_enable_anyway">Actifsr quand même</string>

    <string name="dcc_enable_send_warning_title">Avertissement de sécurité</string>
    <string name="dcc_enable_send_warning_body">DCC is a legacy peer to peer file sharing protocol et the files are sent over an insecure et unencrypted connection. This means that all data sent using the feature can potentially be copied or manipulated by attackers, especially on public WiFi networks.\nAdditionally, due to the protocol\'s nature when you share files using DCC, you are also giving your IP address to the other party. DCC generally does not work when using mobile data, et may not work on some WiFi connections.\n\nBecause of this, we recommend that you instead use 3rd party sharing services et only share a link with the target user instead of DCC.</string>

